      advanced: {
        question: 'What implication does dependent otherness have for the self-other distinction?',
        options: ['A) None', 'B) "Self" depends on "other" and vice versa — the self-other distinction is dependent, not inherent. This is the philosophical foundation of anātman (no-self).', 'C) Self is inherently distinct from other', 'D) Only other is dependent'],
        correct: 'B',
        explanation: 'If otherness is dependent, the self-other distinction is dependent. No inherent self exists independently of other. This is the root of anātman.',
      },
